WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.567
-Thank you. Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.901
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
You're here!

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:09.200
I love that energy.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.968
Guys, we are coming at you
live from New York City,

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:16.634
where there's kind of
a heat wave happening.

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:20.000
It was 82 degrees out today.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.334
82 in October.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.667
On my way to work,
I saw a scarecrow in a Speedo.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:26.834
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:30.968
-It was 82 and sweaty,
which is also how to describe

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.601
Episode 2 of "Golden Bachelor."

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.133
-Ooh!

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:40.634
-Some big news
from Washington today.

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:42.133
For the first time in history,

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:45.400
the House voted
to oust its speaker.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.467
That's right.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:48.767
After only
nine months on the job,

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:52.601
Kevin McCarthy has been removed
as speaker of the House.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:54.234
Yeah, nine months.

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:57.634
Even Aaron Rodgers is like,
"Damn, that was fast."

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:04.167
Nine months? I've been to
Phish concerts longer than that.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:06.734
Anyway, now that McCarthy's
run as speaker is over,

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:08.133
I thought it'd be fun
to take a look back

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.701
at his greatest moments
as Speaker of the House.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:15.901
♪♪

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.501
♪♪
-It was just...

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:22.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:30.000
Well, the other big story is

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.167
Trump's fraud trial
is under way.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:35.501
And after his big day in court,
he posted -- This is real.

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:36.834
He posted this -- I know.

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:38.400
I have to say, "This is real,"
'cause a lot of people

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.601
won't believe that it's real.

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:40.601
It is real.

00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:43.100
He posted a sketch of Jesus

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.334
sitting next to him
in the courtroom.

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:45.534
Take a look at this.

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:47.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:56.334
When Jesus saw what he posted,
he said, "Oh, my dad."

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:58.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:02.667
But did you see this yesterday?

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:04.934
Trump apparently had
a huge McDonald's order

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:06.701
delivered to the courthouse.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.567
This is a photo of the delivery.
Look at it.

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:10.868
-Wow!

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:14.200
-That's not McDonald's delivery.
That's McDonald's luggage.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.567
By the way, Trump eating
McDonald's is not really news,

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:17.901
I don't think.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:20.734
Now, if Trump orders a
quinoa bowl from Sweetgreen --

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:21.834
that's news.

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:23.567
I think that would be...
But get this.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.300
So, Trump complained
that it's unfair

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.601
that his trial
doesn't have a jury.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:29.033
But the reason
it doesn't have a jury

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:31.601
is because his lawyers
never asked for one.

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:33.634
This is true.

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:35.667
To be fair, Trump can't have
a jury of his peers.

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:37.367
I mean, where are they going
to get 12 bankrupt

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:41.100
former reality-show hosts?

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.534
You know it's not good
when you're missing

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:44.601
the legal competence
of Rudy Giuliani.

00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:46.601
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:48.334
Switching gears,
I saw that Paris

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:52.968
is dealing with a citywide
outbreak of bedbugs.

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:57.100
The deputy mayor saying,
"No one is safe."

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.000
And now President
Emmanuel Macron

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.367
is being urged to intervene.

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:03.200
In fact, he asked to appear
on our show tonight

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.934
to shed some light
on the crisis.

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:07.367
Mr. President,
the floor is yours.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:11.667
♪♪

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:13.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:21.400
♪ Bonjour ♪

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.501
♪ It is me ♪

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.901
♪ There are bugs in Paris ♪

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:27.400
♪ That are bigger than fleas ♪

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.234
♪ And they make you itchy ♪

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:32.834
♪ They could be in your sheets ♪

00:03:32.834 --> 00:03:35.334
♪ So check underneath ♪

00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:37.734
♪ And if it were me ♪

00:03:37.734 --> 00:03:41.734
♪ I wouldn't do Airbnb ♪

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:44.334
♪ Anywhere, they could creep ♪

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:46.534
♪ Even chest hair you see ♪

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:50.501
[ Crowd cheering ]
♪ So give it a clean ♪

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:54.133
♪ With a spritz of Febreze ♪

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.734
♪ But it is Fashion Week ♪

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:59.300
♪ Louis V and Gucci ♪

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.801
♪ Full of celebrity ♪

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:05.234
♪ Chalamet, Timothée ♪

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:07.801
♪ He is dating Kylie ♪

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:10.601
♪ And he plays Wonka, Willy ♪

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:12.934
♪ I love his movies ♪

00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:16.167
♪ On the IMDb ♪

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:18.868
♪ But the bedbugs, O-M-G ♪

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:21.367
♪ They are really icky ♪

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:23.400
♪ Everywhere, they will be ♪

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.300
♪ Just like Swift and Kelce ♪

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.501
♪ But for now ♪

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:32.901
♪ I bid you adieu ♪

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:35.767
♪ Adieu, adieu ♪

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:37.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:41.267
♪♪

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:44.634
Thank you. Thank you.
Thank you.

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:48.400
Emmanuel Macron, everybody.
He just ran off.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.100
He ran away.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.601
Bye.

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:56.501
-Oh, he's waving to you.
-He was waving to me.

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:58.033
-Oh!
-Isn't that nice of him?

00:04:58.033 --> 00:05:02.367
-Oh, my gosh. And he sang.
-Oh, my gosh. Take care.

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:03.601
Guys, listen to this.

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:05.367
Delta Air Lines said
that they discovered

00:05:05.367 --> 00:05:08.567
that some of their
aircraft engines had fake parts.

00:05:08.567 --> 00:05:10.868
What?!

00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:12.501
It's weird when you see parts
of your plane

00:05:12.501 --> 00:05:14.067
being built on "Lego Masters."

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:15.434
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:17.033
Yeah, they looked inside
one of their planes

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:19.567
and found a guy just making
engine noises with his mouth.

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:22.167
[ Imitates engine revving ]

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:24.267
"Come on, Larry. Come on."

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:26.200
Yep, their planes had
a lot of fake parts,

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.267
which is why they're going
to be a new cast member

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:30.200
on "Real Housewives
of LaGuardia."

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:36.567
Some more business news.

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:39.834
Chipotle is testing a new robot
that can make burrito bowls

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:41.267
and salads.

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:43.167
It's not really that impressive.

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:45.701
It's just a ladle taped
to a pitching machine.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:50.934
Well, guys, it's very good
to be here. It feels good.

00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:53.334
This is our second show
back after we were on strike,

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:54.501
and it's so --

00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:56.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.934
I'm happy to be here.

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:05.234
We were off the air
for over five months.

00:06:05.234 --> 00:06:09.734
In the five months, I got into
grilling, I started a podcast.

00:06:09.734 --> 00:06:11.067
Higgins,
what did you do this summer?

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:13.300
-I hit the picket lines,
went to Europe.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.634
-Oh, good. That's good.
That's great.

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:16.033
How about you, Quest?

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:18.067
-We went on tour with LL Cool J.

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:19.601
-Oh, that's right.
That was awesome.

00:06:19.601 --> 00:06:20.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:23.834
-Cool.

00:06:23.834 --> 00:06:26.601
How about you, James?
What'd you do this summer?

00:06:26.601 --> 00:06:30.167
-I'm glad you asked, Jimmy.

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:33.667
My summer was totally tubular.

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:37.133
Not. Schwing!

00:06:37.133 --> 00:06:40.267
I was looking forward
to seeing "Barbenheimer."

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:43.300
That's the last name
of my German

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:46.133
pen pal, Helga Barbenheimer.

00:06:46.133 --> 00:06:48.033
But it turns out she isn't real.

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:50.834
I was being catfished by
the rude teens

00:06:50.834 --> 00:06:52.267
who do donuts on my lawn.

00:06:52.267 --> 00:06:53.467
-Alright.

00:06:53.467 --> 00:06:56.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:58.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.868
-But at least I became
fluent in German.

00:07:00.868 --> 00:07:02.901
Get a load of this.

00:07:02.901 --> 00:07:05.701
Oh, my gosh.

00:07:05.901 --> 00:07:07.901
[ Speaking German ]

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:41.400
-What?!

00:07:59.067 --> 00:08:00.868
-What?!

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:19.901
-Oh, come...
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.901 --> 00:08:22.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.400
[ Speaking German ]

00:08:29.334 --> 00:08:33.968
-James, James, James,
are you okay, buddy?

00:08:33.968 --> 00:08:35.901
-James isn't here today.

00:08:35.901 --> 00:08:37.901
Exum disappearium.

00:08:39.567 --> 00:08:41.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:46.834 --> 00:08:48.334
-The writers' strike hit
some of us

00:08:48.334 --> 00:08:50.767
harder than others, I think.

00:08:50.767 --> 00:08:51.901
Give it up for
James Poyser, everybody.

00:08:51.901 --> 00:08:53.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:56.501 --> 00:08:57.801
Well, this is wild.

00:08:57.801 --> 00:09:00.667
A man in Slovakia was fined
after a traffic camera

00:09:00.667 --> 00:09:05.567
caught his car speeding
with his dog behind the wheel.

00:09:05.667 --> 00:09:09.634
Yeah, meanwhile, his owner was
in the back humping a pillow.

00:09:09.634 --> 00:09:11.200
The dog was like,
"I've got to go get

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.734
to the matinee of 'Paw Patrol.'"

00:09:13.734 --> 00:09:16.033
Hey, guys,
I read about a 77-year-old man

00:09:16.033 --> 00:09:17.400
at a retirement community
in Florida

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:20.100
who is facing charges
for his stockpile

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:23.033
of illegal
erectile-dysfunction drugs.

00:09:23.033 --> 00:09:25.934
Yeah, legal experts say he could
face a very stiff sentence.

00:09:25.934 --> 00:09:27.267
-Whoa!
-Whoa!

00:09:27.267 --> 00:09:30.133
-If found guilty, he's looking
at 20 years of hard time.

00:09:30.133 --> 00:09:31.834
-Aah!

00:09:31.834 --> 00:09:33.367
-In court, the bailiff said,
"All rise,"

00:09:33.367 --> 00:09:34.701
and the guy was like,
"Way ahead of you."

00:09:34.701 --> 00:09:36.267
Alright.

00:09:36.267 --> 00:09:38.701
Guys, finally, it is Tuesday.

00:09:38.701 --> 00:09:41.434
It is time for "WePost."
Here we go.

00:09:41.434 --> 00:09:45.200
-♪ WePost ♪

00:09:46.234 --> 00:09:47.300
♪ WePost ♪

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:49.167
-Alright. Welcome.

00:09:49.167 --> 00:09:50.868
Welcome to "WePost."

00:09:50.868 --> 00:09:57.000
This is where we, as a group,

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:00.868
decide something
we should post on X.

00:10:00.868 --> 00:10:02.734
I'm going to show you
five different posts,

00:10:02.734 --> 00:10:03.734
and we're all going to vote

00:10:03.734 --> 00:10:04.901
on whether you like
each one or not.

00:10:04.901 --> 00:10:06.701
You all have voting clickers
at your seats.

00:10:06.701 --> 00:10:07.968
You should at least.

00:10:07.968 --> 00:10:10.033
If you don't, let us know,
and we'll get you one.

00:10:10.033 --> 00:10:12.534
You can vote for all of these,
you can vote for none of them,

00:10:12.534 --> 00:10:14.667
whatever you want,
and we'll see the results live.

00:10:14.667 --> 00:10:16.167
Higgins, Roots,
you have clickers?

00:10:16.167 --> 00:10:17.167
-Got it.
-Roots, you have clickers?

00:10:17.167 --> 00:10:18.400
-We got 'em.
-Alright. Very good.

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:20.634
Whatever post gets
the most likes,

00:10:20.634 --> 00:10:22.634
we will post it out
live on the show

00:10:22.634 --> 00:10:25.701
so you can all like it
and we can "wepost" it.

00:10:25.701 --> 00:10:27.901
It's like a shared experience.
You guys ready for this?

00:10:27.901 --> 00:10:30.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Alright, good.

00:10:30.033 --> 00:10:32.100
The first post is...

00:10:36.901 --> 00:10:40.467
♪♪
-Wow!

00:10:40.467 --> 00:10:45.634
-Again, the writers have been on
strike for north of five months.

00:10:46.934 --> 00:10:49.000
Alright. It's interesting.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.801
A lot of people have their
phones out during the concerts.

00:10:50.801 --> 00:10:52.567
They don't watch
the show themselves.

00:10:52.567 --> 00:10:54.367
-They just watch the thing.
-That's correct. Yeah.

00:10:54.367 --> 00:10:57.968
So it's more of an observation
than a joke.

00:10:57.968 --> 00:11:00.868
Sure. The votes are in.
Let's see the results here.

00:11:01.534 --> 00:11:04.734
Wow!
[ Sad tuba, cymbal crash ]

00:11:04.734 --> 00:11:06.801
Very honest,
very honest audience.

00:11:06.801 --> 00:11:08.767
[ Laughter ]

00:11:08.767 --> 00:11:10.734
Very honest tonight.

00:11:10.734 --> 00:11:12.934
Okay.

00:11:12.934 --> 00:11:14.934
This next one is...

00:11:18.334 --> 00:11:19.501
[ Laughter ]

00:11:19.501 --> 00:11:24.367
♪♪

00:11:24.367 --> 00:11:26.567
It's like walking on the moon.

00:11:26.567 --> 00:11:28.567
-Uneven. They're not to code.

00:11:28.567 --> 00:11:29.868
-I can't be the only one.

00:11:29.868 --> 00:11:31.701
Let's see the results
right here.

00:11:31.701 --> 00:11:32.934
[ Drumroll ]

00:11:32.934 --> 00:11:35.434
Alright. A little bit better.
Alright, not bad.

00:11:36.267 --> 00:11:38.701
-Yeah. Yeah.
-I want to remind everyone,

00:11:38.701 --> 00:11:40.300
these don't necessarily
get better.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:41.801
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.801 --> 00:11:43.467
That's the thing
about this game.

00:11:43.467 --> 00:11:45.000
That might be it.
-You don't know what's coming.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:46.767
-I have no idea
if it's going to get better.

00:11:46.767 --> 00:11:48.601
I don't know if it does.
-Ready?

00:11:48.601 --> 00:11:49.701
-But let's try
this next one here.

00:11:49.701 --> 00:11:50.701
This next one here says...

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:58.367
[ Laughter ]

00:11:58.367 --> 00:12:00.534
♪♪

00:12:00.534 --> 00:12:03.834
Just see what happens.
-Yeah.

00:12:03.834 --> 00:12:06.834
-"Hey, enough here for two."
-Yeah.

00:12:06.834 --> 00:12:09.701
Maybe you can tape
a concert with your phone, yeah.

00:12:09.701 --> 00:12:11.667
-Alright, let's see the results.

00:12:11.667 --> 00:12:13.133
I have a good feeling
about this one. Let's see.

00:12:13.133 --> 00:12:14.801
Oh! That's good!

00:12:14.801 --> 00:12:17.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:17.501 --> 00:12:19.133
Just see what happens.
Why not?

00:12:19.133 --> 00:12:20.767
Alright, let's go.

00:12:20.767 --> 00:12:22.200
Next one up, it says...

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.167
[ Laughter ]

00:12:27.167 --> 00:12:29.400
♪♪

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:31.000
They're all in the bed together.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.467
-He's faking it.
-The whole room's a bed, right?

00:12:32.467 --> 00:12:33.567
-Yeah.

00:12:35.367 --> 00:12:37.734
Finds a golden ticket.
-You went yes?

00:12:37.734 --> 00:12:38.734
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:12:38.734 --> 00:12:39.834
You go yes on all of them,
right?

00:12:39.834 --> 00:12:41.467
-Yes, I do.

00:12:41.467 --> 00:12:42.701
-Did you go yes
on that first one?

00:12:42.701 --> 00:12:44.300
-Yes.
-Wow.

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:45.901
-I did not.
-That's interesting.

00:12:45.901 --> 00:12:47.534
-You did not?
-No, I'm honest.

00:12:47.534 --> 00:12:49.033
-You're honest. Yeah.
-Unless it gets in my way.

00:12:49.033 --> 00:12:50.400
-He's honest
but he's very positive.

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:51.534
-Yeah.

00:12:51.534 --> 00:12:53.033
-Did you go yes on that one?
-Yeah.

00:12:53.033 --> 00:12:54.801
-So, yeah, I went yes
on that one, as well.

00:12:54.801 --> 00:12:55.868
-Yeah.
-It's pretty funny.

00:12:55.868 --> 00:12:57.400
But I think the other one
is still --

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.501
-Might be better.
-I think the other one's better.

